# hand-reviewed 2026-10-28 against the fixture, the compiler call-chain oracle and the runtime trace: R18 on POST routes: the provider middleware, then the library json validator (zValidator; the built-in validator with a hand-written check), then the handler, which reads the validated body and calls the service it reads out of the context; service -> repository -> db. The body rows are the JSON each request carries: without them the validator answers 400 and no handler runs (checked). The middleware -> handler hop runs through the validator, which awaits the body before it calls next, so it is observed as both functions running in a one-request run, the handler entered from library code
